   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Data Science & Machine Learning with Python\n",
    "\n",
    "This guide demonstrates how **kyar-kyar** automatically converts Jupyter Notebooks (`.ipynb` and `.ipyb`) into rich, beautifully formatted static blog posts and documentation.\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setting Up the Environment\n",
    "\n",
    "First, we initialize our Python environment and import the scientific computing libraries:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Environment initialized successfully.\n",
      "NumPy Version: 1.26.4\n",
      "Pandas Version: 2.2.2\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Environment initialized successfully.\")\n",
    "print(f\"NumPy Version: {np.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Pandas Version: {pd.__version__}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Generating Synthetic Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "We create a dataset containing performance metrics across multiple cloud deployment regions:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/html": [
       "<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th>Region</th>\n      <th>Requests/sec</th>\n      <th>Latency (ms)</th>\n      <th>Uptime (%)</th>\n      <th>Health</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>us-east-1</td>\n      <td>14,250</td>\n      <td>18.4</td>\n      <td>99.98%</td>\n      <td>Optimal</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>us-west-2</td>\n      <td>9,820</td>\n      <td>22.1</td>\n      <td>99.95%</td>\n      <td>Optimal</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>eu-central-1</td>\n      <td>11,400</td>\n      <td>24.6</td>\n      <td>99.99%</td>\n      <td>Optimal</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>ap-southeast-1</td>\n      <td>7,630</td>\n      <td>31.2</td>\n      <td>99.92%</td>\n      <td>Optimal</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "          Region  Requests/sec  Latency (ms)  Uptime (%)   Health\n",
       "0      us-east-1         14250          18.4       99.98  Optimal\n",
       "1      us-west-2          9820          22.1       99.95  Optimal\n",
       "2   eu-central-1         11400          24.6       99.99  Optimal\n",
       "3  ap-southeast-1          7630          31.2       99.92  Optimal"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 2,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "data = {\n",
    "    'Region': ['us-east-1', 'us-west-2', 'eu-central-1', 'ap-southeast-1'],\n",
    "    'Requests/sec': [14250, 9820, 11400, 7630],\n",
    "    'Latency (ms)': [18.4, 22.1, 24.6, 31.2],\n",
    "    'Uptime (%)': ['99.98%', '99.95%', '99.99%', '99.92%'],\n",
    "    'Health': ['Optimal', 'Optimal', 'Optimal', 'Optimal']\n",
    "}\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(data)\n",
    "df"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Visualizing Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "Below is the visualized chart generated directly from matplotlib output in the notebook:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/svg+xml": [
       "<svg width=\"100%\" height=\"160\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 160\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"background: transparent; border-radius: 8px;\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"560\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <rect x=\"80\" y=\"40\" width=\"60\" height=\"90\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#6366f1\" fill-opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n  <text x=\"110\" y=\"148\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"currentColor\" fill-opacity=\"0.7\" text-anchor=\"middle\">US-East</text>\n  <text x=\"110\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\">14.2k</text>\n  <rect x=\"200\" y=\"65\" width=\"60\" height=\"65\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#6366f1\" fill-opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"148\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"currentColor\" fill-opacity=\"0.7\" text-anchor=\"middle\">US-West</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"57\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9.8k</text>\n  <rect x=\"320\" y=\"55\" width=\"60\" height=\"75\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#6366f1\" fill-opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n  <text x=\"350\" y=\"148\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"currentColor\" fill-opacity=\"0.7\" text-anchor=\"middle\">EU-Central</text>\n  <text x=\"350\" y=\"47\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\">11.4k</text>\n  <rect x=\"440\" y=\"80\" width=\"60\" height=\"50\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#6366f1\" fill-opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n  <text x=\"470\" y=\"148\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"currentColor\" fill-opacity=\"0.7\" text-anchor=\"middle\">AP-SE</text>\n  <text x=\"470\" y=\"72\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\">7.6k</text>\n</svg>"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 600x160 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Render chart\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 2.5))\n",
    "plt.title('Requests per Second by Region')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Summary & Wikilinks\n",
    "\n",
    "Notice how seamless the notebook conversion is:\n",
    "- Markdown headings appear in the **Table of Contents**.\n",
    "- Code inputs and outputs are styled with syntax highlighting.\n",
    "- You can link from notebooks to other notes using [[guides/getting-started|Getting Started]] or [[guides/theming-and-customization|Theming]]!"
   ]
  }
 ],
